  "summary": "Verified the existing panel's editor: the visualization picker for \"{{v6}}\" already showed \"Stat\", so no change was needed. Back on the dashboard I used Add > Visualization and picked \"Text\" in the visualization picker, set the panel title to exactly \"{{v3}} Notes\" and put the markdown \"{{v7}}\\n\\nBench run {{v3}} — created via automation.\" into the text content editor (value read back verbatim from the editor). Saving produced a \"Dashboard saved\" status alert and exiting edit mode raised no \"Discard changes\" prompt, confirming a clean saved state. In view mode the dashboard shows both panels — \"{{v3}} Notes\" (with the rendered paragraph \"{{v5}} run {{v3}} — created via automation.\") and \"{{v6}}\" (Stat value 54.3) — at http://127.0.0.1:3000/d/{{v1}}/{{v2}}.",
